<title>UK: INSIGHT -Stg/mark seen holding 3.0510 support.</title>
<headline>INSIGHT -Stg/mark seen holding 3.0510 support.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sterling has eased slightly and will be cushioned around immediate support of 3.0510 marks, said chartists.</p>
<p>&quot;Sterling/mark was taken down near immediate support around 3.0510. I think the short-term aim is to range between 3.0510/70,&quot; said Robin Poynder, chief foreign exchange dealer at Charterhouse.</p>
<p>At 0735 GMT sterling/mark was at 3.0558/68 against 3.0560/70 in late Europe on Friday, and above early lows of 3.0519 marks.</p>
<p>Poynder said while initial support around 3.0510 marks should hold, the next important level is 3.0450 marks.</p>
</text>
